{{also|fivér|Fiver}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈfaɪvɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-fiver.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪvə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[banknote]] with a value of five units of currency.
#: ''Do you have a '''fiver''' I could borrow? I can pay you back tomorrow.''
# {{lb|en|slang|by extension}} The value in money that this represents.
#: ''I bought the chocolates; they were only a '''fiver'''.''
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} A clenched fist.
#: {{synonyms|en|bunch of fives}}
# A mathematical puzzle played on a 5 &times; 5 grid.
# {{lb|en|Islam}} A [[Zaydi]] Shiite Muslim, who disagrees with the majority of Shiites on the identity of the Fifth Imam.
# {{lb|en|religion}} A person who gives five percent of their income or five hours a week of their time to charity (a reduction of ten percent [[tithing]]).

